        {
          "data": {
            "lookup_key": "movie_summer_spotlight_body",
            "type": "text",
            "text": "<p>From Marvel to Wes Anderson, the summer of 2025 brings an unusually strong mix of blockbusters and prestige films.</p><h3>The big ones</h3><p>Mission: Impossible delivers the franchise finale everyone has been waiting for. The Fantastic Four: First Steps resets the MCU timeline with a refreshing retro-futuristic approach. Superman reintroduces DC's icon under James Gunn's steady hand.</p><h3>The surprises</h3><p>The Phoenician Scheme brings Wes Anderson's most elaborate visual puzzle to screen, while Nonnas — based on a true story — is the comedy the summer needed.</p><h3>For the whole family</h3><p>How to Train Your Dragon's live-action remake and The Bad Guys 2 make this a summer worth hitting the cinema with the kids.</p>",
